-- Ekwo OS — The Gambia: chart of accounts, journals, taxes and defaults.
--
-- Generated from packs/gm at version 0.1.0, do not edit.
-- Change the pack and run `ekwo pack build gm`; `ekwo pack check --all`
-- refuses a seed that is not the exact output of its pack, and the CI runs it.
--
-- Community pack — not reviewed.
-- Written from:
--   Value Added Tax Brochure — what VAT is; the standard rate of 15 % and the zero rate on exports (§ 2); how VAT is calculated on a VAT-inclusive price (§ 4); the exempted supplies (§ 6); compulsory registration from D2,000,000 of taxable supplies in a tax year and voluntary registration from D1,000,000 (§ 7); de-registration (§ 9); monthly filing and payment on the 15th of the following month and import VAT payable before release (§ 10); refunds (§ 12). It states that it is not an exhaustive replacement of the VAT laws. (Gambia Revenue Authority)
--     https://gra.gm/download-file/8d0cfa28-d217-11ed-9b31-029254d29bb1
--   Domestic Taxes FAQs, VAT section — standard rate 15 %, zero rate on exports of goods and services, thresholds of D2,000,000 (compulsory) and D1,000,000 (voluntary) of taxable supplies in a tax year, monthly return due 15 days after the month end, filing at the nearest Domestic Taxes Department office, payment at a DTD office or a partner bank, input VAT credit and refunds (Gambia Revenue Authority)
--     https://www.gra.gm/domestic-faqs
--   GRA Online Services — the Authority's page for its electronic services; it links the tax calculators and the Domestic Taxes Department, and does not itself name a VAT return filing function (Gambia Revenue Authority)
--     https://www.gra.gm/online-services
--   Use of IFRS Standards by jurisdiction — The Gambia: IFRS Standards required for commercial banks and permitted for all other companies; IFRS for SMEs not adopted but SMEs are permitted to use it; the Companies Act 1955 does not specify the accounting standards; the Gambia Institute of Chartered Accountants and the Financial Reporting Oversight Board established by a 2013 Act (profile last updated 16 June 2016) (IFRS Foundation)
--     https://www.ifrs.org/use-around-the-world/use-of-ifrs-standards-by-jurisdiction/view-jurisdiction/gambia/
--
-- Reference data: `install_country_template()` copies it into a company,
-- nothing here belongs to a company.

